  "conclusion": "The normal-fine variant reduced local normal-component RMSE by about 19–30% relative to the equal-step weighted tangent coder, while tangential-component RMSE rose about 9–12%. It was about 0.75–1.02% larger in aggregate than weighted tangent for each ordering. It is a targeted rate-distortion trade-off, not a total-size win. On these synthetic meshes, adaptive MO3D encoded to 25,807 bytes versus 28,275 bytes for Draco selected under the same per-mesh conservative max-error ceiling, but Draco was substantially faster and often had lower actual reconstruction error. These results do not establish a general win over Draco."
